
# Technical Support System Dataset

## Overview
This folder contains the raw dataset used for analyzing IT support team performance. The dataset includes information related to support tickets, agents, resolution time, SLA compliance, and customer feedback.

## Dataset Description
The dataset contains the following important fields:

- Ticket ID – Unique identifier for each support ticket
- Status – Current status of the ticket (Open, Resolved, Closed)
- Priority – Level of urgency assigned to the ticket
- Source – Channel through which the ticket was created (Email, Phone, Chat)
- Topic – Type of issue reported by the customer
- Agent Group – Support team responsible for handling the ticket
- Agent Name – Name of the assigned support agent
- Created Time – Time when the ticket was created
- Resolution Time – Time when the issue was resolved
- Close Time – Time when the ticket was closed
- SLA For Resolution – Indicates whether the ticket resolution met SLA requirements
- Agent Interactions – Number of interactions between agent and customer
- Survey Results – Customer satisfaction rating after issue resolution
- Product Group – Category of product related to the issue
- Support Level – Tier level of support (Tier 1, Tier 2, etc.)
- Country – Customer location
- Latitude & Longitude – Geographic coordinates of the customer location

## Purpose of the Dataset
This dataset is used to analyze:

- IT support team performance
- Ticket resolution efficiency
- SLA compliance
- Customer satisfaction trends
- Support workload distribution

## Note
This is the raw dataset and may contain missing values or inconsistencies that will be handled during the data preprocessing stage.
